  "discussions_data": [
    {
      "id": "b6f3a364c12b31ae8af12ae9ef3c0bfe10d3d500",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1581694313,
          "type": null,
          "body": "The rough C11 (and C99?) equivalent of the `G_GUINT64_CONSTANT()` macro appears to be `UINT64_C()`, although, to quote C11 7.20.4.1 \"Macros for minimum-width integer constants\":\n\n> The macro `INT`*N*`_C(`*value*`)` shall expand to an integer constant expression corresponding to the type `int_least`*N*`_t`. The macro `UINT`*N*`_C(`*value*`)` shall expand to an integer constant expression corresponding to the type `uint_least`*N*`_t`. For example, if `uint_least64_t` is a name for the type `unsigned long long int`, then `UINT64_C(0x123)` might expand to the integer constant `0x123ULL`.\n\nSo `UINT64_C()` is for `uint_least64_t`; however, on the platforms we support, we can probably expect `uint64_t` to be the the same type as `uint_least64_t`.",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/guyharris"
          },
          "created_at": "2023-09-28T07:15:00.624Z",
          "updated_at": "2023-09-28T07:15:00.624Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 253633372,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 12313,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ba7fc9c05e5e330456baab3e4609f26cdeeeb777",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1582631943,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Currently there are 4 occurrences of `UINT64_C()` in our codebase (excluding generated and external include files). That means 427 occurrences of `G_GUINT64_CONSTANT()` to go. That would be a separate campaign.\n\nFor now I would suggest keeping `#include glib.h` localized in the files that use the features provided by it, until they have been converted.",
          "author": {
            "id": 2398962,
            "username": "JaapKeuter",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Jaap Keuter",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/722b0c520542a23cb8f8ea7070a45c88f9e9214dc700ac151e419e9649e0304e?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/JaapKeuter"
          },
          "created_at": "2023-09-28T16:40:17.451Z",
          "updated_at": "2023-09-28T16:40:17.451Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 253633372,
